            "notes": "Now you really start to hurt the enemies. You want to play at the longest range you realistically can while still hitting your main source of ability damage, whether it be your upgraded [Whip Shot](ability_b11d31d7-cf58-4e0d-8ec8-fbde3af5bb04) or [Sk\u00f6ldkastning](item_a6c36dee-d961-428b-b27c-93ba5ef377d8). \n\nYour [Whip Shot](ability_b11d31d7-cf58-4e0d-8ec8-fbde3af5bb04) should now have just over 30m range, vs just over 25m for [Sk\u00f6ldkastning](item_a6c36dee-d961-428b-b27c-93ba5ef377d8). \n\n---\n\n### POWER\nAlways take [God Ray](item_4abb5cdb-f113-4f21-aa0a-e67d95a11fd0) this round, regardless of what you picked as your first power. It'll affect either of them, and is what really lets you do big chunks of damage. \n\n---\n\n### ITEMS\n[Chain Extender](item_0a0d50dc-0ec9-42f6-a0ad-c373eb44dc6d) is *great* with [Maces to Faces](item_072c4780-53a1-4abd-9fc9-32406c3b7b49) and [God Ray](item_4abb5cdb-f113-4f21-aa0a-e67d95a11fd0). This'll even let you damage flyers like [Freja](hero_e80840a1-845d-4008-966c-585b7cb4a424) and [Pharah](hero_0baf7420-ff13-4b92-81f7-ca21b61dacf9) when they're up in the sky. \n\nIf you're facing multiple flyers, or one really annoying one that's doing a lot against your team, try taking [Skyline Nanites](item_0b334927-da04-42d6-8dfd-96e7b6c1cd51) to hit them for even bigger damage.\n\nThat being said, if you took [Sk\u00f6ldkastning](item_a6c36dee-d961-428b-b27c-93ba5ef377d8) first round, you won't have near the same accuracy with [Whip Shot](ability_b11d31d7-cf58-4e0d-8ec8-fbde3af5bb04), so take [Scavenged Steel](item_fb9d2d13-db05-46fa-b3c6-07495b1872a4) instead of [Chain Extender](item_0a0d50dc-0ec9-42f6-a0ad-c373eb44dc6d) for fast ults, as damage from your Shield Boomerang counts as \"ability damage\". If you do this, I recommend also grabbing [Charged Plating](item_b8ca58e7-6ae2-40ee-8618-fe2f32315295). \n\nKeep both of these items until round 5, then follow the build.",
